{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415060-the-people\u2019s-republic-of-val-verde-a-sandbox-satrapy","id":1415060,"title":"The People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde: A Sandbox Satrapy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-22T06:38:51-07:00","id":1415060,"title":"The People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde: A Sandbox Satrapy","content":"I found this on my computer. I used it for a two-day 2nd edition game some years ago.<br /> <br /> If I am not mistaken, in that particular game, one of the Winglords may have been a PC and there may have been an inciting incident involving the Satrap getting horribly sick, blaming the All-Seeing Eye for this.<br /> <br /> Anyway, maybe someone will be able to use it for something in their games.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Satrapy of Val Verde, Realm Year 768</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>History:</b><br /> The island kingdom of Val Verde was first established as a satrapy in Realm Year 327 when explorers discovered deposits of green jade in the jungle of the island kingdom. The first satrap of Val Verde \u2013 a grandson of Ragara \u2013 was allowed to mine the precious magical material in return for ridding the island of a tribe of howler-monkey beastmen that the local King found himself feuding with.<br /> <br /> The green jade deposits of the Val Verde were mined to the point of depletion in a matter of a few decades, and in the century that followed Val Verde continued as a satrapy in name more than anything, paying only a token tax.<br /> <br /> This changed in Realm Year 465 with the Unbroken Rushes Rebellion on the Blessed Isle and the resulting food shortage. The Satrap of Val Verde at this point \u2013 Nellens Monosashi \u2013 saw an untapped agricultural potential in the fertile island kingdom. If the fertile land of Val Verde could be cultivated and used for banana plantations, it would present a cheap and nutritious resource for the Realm in general and for legions stationed in the West in particular.<br /> <br /> The King of Val Verde did not agree with the proposal \u2013 his people were hunters, gatherers, warriors, and fishermen; they were not farmers \u2013 so Nellens Monosashi had to work around him.<br /> <br /> Through his allies in the Immaculate Order Nellens Monosashi courted a local banana god and through his allies in the All-Seeing Eye he supplied the people of Val Verde with weapons and anti-royalist propaganda.<br /> <br /> The revolution came and the Kingdom of Val Verde gave way to the People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde. The revolutionary leader \u2013 Unkou the Red \u2013 had barely been elected as the country\u2019s first Chancellor before he declared the country\u2019s partnership with Satrap Nellens Monosashi and with the newly-established Imperial Fruit Company.<br /> <br /> <b>Current Situation:</b><br /> The Thirty-Second Imperial Legion was spread across several satrapies of the West in Realm Year 764 when its commander \u2013 General Cynis Senshu \u2013 received the still unofficial report that his forces were to be disbanded. Gathering his three most unquestionably loyal Winglords around him in the Satrapy of Val Verde, General Cynis Senshu ordered the remaining 17 wings to return home to the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> Striking a deal with Peleps Daraku of the Imperial Fruit Company and using his legionnaires-turned-mercenaries as political leverage, Cynis Senshu could soon replace the title of General with that of Satrap. Cathak Haisha who had been the Satrap of Val Verde up until then was put in house arrest by Magistrate Nellens Nori.<br /> <br /> Several Cathak Senators have raised the issue in the Deliberative, but for the most part Realm officials have turned a blind eye on the coup. Pragmatics reason that there is little benefit in risking to upset the steady flow of taxes, the low prices on bananas, and the socio-political stability in the region by trying to remove Satrap Cynis Senshu and re-instating Cathak Haisha. Conspiracy theorists suspect that the coup may have been backed by the All-Seeing Eye. After all, how did the General know not to return to the Blessed Isle to have his Legion disbanded?<br /> <br /> <b>Main exports:</b><br /> Bananas and green jade<br /> <br /> <b>Local Government:</b><br /> Sen\u2019Ou, Chancellor of the People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants the old Satrap back or independence from the Realm</span><br /> <br /> General Oomaka, Defense and Freedom Minister of the People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">- <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wants to become the new Chancellor and want independence from the Realm</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Baibai, Trade and Riches Minister of the People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">- <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wants to become filthy rich</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Bunmei, Bread and Circus Minister of the People\u2019s Republic of Val Verde<br /> <br /> <b>Official Realm Presence:</b><br /> Cynis Senshu, Satrap of Val Verde<br /> <br /> Peleps Daraku, representative of the Imperial Fruit Company</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants trade, money, riches</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Nellens Nori, Imperial Magistrate</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants power, money, sex, the favor of the Empress</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Little Palm, Immaculate Monk</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Observes strict adherence to the Immaculate Faith; wants to get rid of Ripe Fruit</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ripe Fruit, Immaculate Monk</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Is a hedonist</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Mercenary Troops of the Satrap:</b><br /> Winglord Cynis Batok<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Favors Cynis Senshu as Satrap of Val Verde</span><br /> <br /> Winglord Nellens Buben</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">- <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Wants to become the new Satrap</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Winglord Peleps Heitai</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants to become the new Satrap</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Ambassadors:</b><br /> Wakame Seaweed, Ambassador of Skullstone</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants religious acceptance for ancestor cults and favorable trade agreements with Skullstone</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Kaikaku, Ambassador of the Neck<br /> <br /> Sango, Ambassador of the Coral Archipelago</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants to usurp Val Verde into the Coral Empire; wants Akiudo arrested for his crimes against Coral</span> </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Notable Gods:</b><br /> Kaiki, God of Val Verde<br /> <br /> Kinomi, local banana god<br /> <br /> Janguru, local jungle god<br /> <br /> The Hanged Plantation Worker, ancestor spirit and revolutionary icon<br /> <br /> <b>Other Notables:</b><br /> Cathak Haisha, former Satrap of Val Verde currently in house arrest</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants to become Satrap again</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ragara Jouingiin, exiled Realm Senator</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Wants to play politics and be a power broker</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">Ma-Chanto, representative of the Guild<br /> <br /> Akiudo, representative of the Western Trade Alliance<br /> <br /> <b>Other Factors:</b><br /> Peleps Paire-Tsu, representative of the Water Fleet</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":864,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","user":"Jutlander","date":". 09-22-2020, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T07:12:23-07:00","id":1415064,"title":"","content":"Very cool banana republic.<br /> <br /> Minor nitpick being that in 3E the West is rather newly explored, so a four-hundred year old Satrapy is probably a bit much. But it's easily fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020